.TH OROC-UPDATE-INIT 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.0" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-update\-init \- Scaffold a minimal update manifest JSON file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc update init [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Scaffold a minimal update manifest JSON file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
use an explicit oro.toml/oro.ini file when deriving defaults
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest\-name=<name>\fR
filename for the manifest JSON (default: manifest.json or ORO_UPDATE_MANIFEST_FILENAME)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.PP
The generated manifest includes these defaults.
.IP \(bu 2
schemaVersion = 1
.IP \(bu 2
appId derived from your oro.toml ([meta] bundle_identifier, falling back to "com.example.app")
.IP \(bu 2
generatedAt = current UTC timestamp
.IP \(bu 2
channels = [update_channel or "stable"]
.IP \(bu 2
updates = a single entry for the current version/channel (with an empty targets array)
.PP
Edit the generated file to add real targets, artifact metadata, or additional updates.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc update init\fR
create ./manifest.json using oro.toml metadata
.TP
\fBoroc update init \-\-manifest\-name app\-updates.json\fR
create ./app\-updates.json instead of manifest.json
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-update(1)
